# Who has to approve a change before it can land on main.
#
# Everything is owned by @sirsjg and @thebulklord. The `main` ruleset requires
# a code owner's review on every pull request, so an outside contributor's work
# cannot merge without one. The repository admin keeps a bypass; the release
# job gets past the ruleset with RELEASE_TOKEN instead, since a user-owned
# repository cannot name the Actions app as a bypass actor.
#
# A code owner has to have write access to the repository, or GitHub ignores
# the entry and never requests their review.
#
# Ownership is by path, last match wins. Narrow the list here before handing
# out write access, not after.

* @sirsjg @thebulklord
